Raise the quality-layer limit of hayro-jpeg2000 0.4.0 from 32 to 255.

JPEG 2000 allows up to 65535 layers, and TIFFs written by JJ2000 (e.g. the
IDR OME-TIFFs this decoder was added for) use 33. The decoder stores the
layer count in a `u8` and keeps layers in a `Vec`, so nothing else depends
on the limit; decoded tiles match OpenJPEG exactly.

--- a/src/j2c/codestream.rs
+++ b/src/j2c/codestream.rs
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 use crate::error::{MarkerError, Result, ValidationError, bail, err};
 use crate::reader::BitReader;
 
-const MAX_LAYER_COUNT: u8 = 32;
+const MAX_LAYER_COUNT: u8 = 255;
 const MAX_RESOLUTION_COUNT: u8 = 32;
 const MAX_PRECINCT_EXPONENT: u8 = 31;
 
